Building easylzma
=================

Requirements:

  * CMake 3.20 or newer
  * A C99 compiler
  * Ninja when using the included presets

Configure and build with CMake presets:

  cmake --preset release
  cmake --build --preset release-build --parallel
  ctest --preset release-test

Or use the standard CMake workflow:

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build --parallel
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

To include a real OTA firmware in the streaming integration test:

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
    -DEASYLZMA_OTA_FIRMWARE=/path/to/firmware.bin
  cmake --build build --parallel
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -R ota-stream

The command-line tools and versioned library bundle are written to:

  build/easylzma-0.0.8/

Install into a custom prefix:

  cmake --install build/release --prefix /path/to/prefix

Installed CMake packages can be consumed with:

  find_package(easylzma 0.0 REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(my_program PRIVATE easylzma::easylzma)

Use easylzma::easylzma for the shared library and
easylzma::easylzma_s for the static library.
